questions.question:
A job-search panel keeps its request state in three variables and renders with:

if (error) return <ErrorBanner />;
if (isLoading) return <Spinner />;
return <Results items={data} />;

The loader is:

async function load(query) {
  isLoading = true;
  try {
    data = await api.search(query);
  } catch (e) {
    error = e;
  } finally {
    isLoading = false;
  }
}

The user searches 'plumber' and the request fails. They search 'electrician' and that request succeeds. What does the panel show?
